          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Learning Objectives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "By the end of this lesson, you should be able to:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Understand what surface area means and how it differs from volume"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Identify the faces of cuboids and triangular prisms"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Calculate the surface area of a cuboid"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Calculate the surface area of a triangular prism"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Apply surface area calculations to real-world problems"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Introduction"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Surface area is the total area of all the faces of a 3D shape. It tells you how much material you would need to cover or wrap the shape. Think about wrapping a gift box (cuboid) or making a tent (triangular prism) -- you need to know the surface area to determine how much paper or fabric is required."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "horizontalRule"
      },
      {
        "type": "visualizationEmbed",
        "attrs": {
          "visualizationId": "math-surface-area-3d",
          "displayMode": "expanded",
          "customHeight": 500
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "quizEmbed",
        "attrs": {
          "quizId": "check-surface-area-prisms"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Key Concepts"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Surface area",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is the total area of all external faces of a 3D shape. It is measured in "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "square units",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " (cm$^2$, m$^2$, etc.)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "prism",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is a 3D shape with a uniform cross-section along its length. The two end faces are identical, and the remaining faces are rectangles."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Surface Area of a Cuboid"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A cuboid has 6 rectangular faces. With length $l$, width $w$, and height $h$:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "$$SA = 2lw + 2lh + 2wh = 2(lw + lh + wh)$$"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Surface Area of a Cube"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A cube has 6 identical square faces of side $s$:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "$$SA = 6s^2$$"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Surface Area of a Triangular Prism"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A triangular prism has:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "2 triangular end faces"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "3 rectangular side faces"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "$$SA = 2 \\times \\text{(area of triangular end)} + \\text{(perimeter of triangle)} \\times \\text{length}$$"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Or simply: add up the areas of all 5 faces."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "horizontalRule"
      },
      {
        "type": "quizEmbed",
        "attrs": {
          "quizId": "check-surface-area-prisms-2"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Worked Examples"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Example 1: Surface Area of a Cuboid"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Question:",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " Find the surface area of a cuboid with length 8 cm, width 5 cm, and height 3 cm."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Solution:",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "$$\\begin{aligned} SA &= 2(lw + lh + wh) \\\\ &= 2(8 \\times 5 + 8 \\times 3 + 5 \\times 3) \\\\ &= 2(40 + 24 + 15) \\\\ &= 2 \\times 79 \\\\ &= 158 \\text{ cm}^2 \\end{aligned}$$"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "horizontalRule"
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Example 2: Surface Area of a Cube"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Question:",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " A cube has side length 4.5 cm. Find its surface area."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Solution:",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "$$\\begin{aligned} SA &= 6s^2 \\\\ &= 6 \\times 4.5^2 \\\\ &= 6 \\times 20.25 \\\\ &= 121.5 \\text{ cm}^2 \\end{aligned}$$"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "horizontalRule"
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Example 3: Triangular Prism"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Question:",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " A triangular prism has a triangular cross-section with base 6 cm, height 4 cm, and two slant sides each 5 cm. The prism is 10 cm long. Find the surface area."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Solution:",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " Area of each triangular end:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "$$A_{\\text{triangle}} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 6 \\times 4 = 12 \\text{ cm}^2$$"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Two triangular ends:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "$$2 \\times 12 = 24 \\text{ cm}^2$$"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Three rectangular faces:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Bottom: $6 \\times 10 = 60$ cm$^2$"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Left slant: $5 \\times 10 = 50$ cm$^2$"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Right slant: $5 \\times 10 = 50$ cm$^2$"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Total rectangular area: $60 + 50 + 50 = 160$ cm$^2$"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "$$\\begin{aligned} SA &= 24 + 160 \\\\ &= 184 \\text{ cm}^2 \\end{aligned}$$"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "horizontalRule"
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Example 4: Open-Top Box"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Question:",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " A cardboard box with no lid has length 30 cm, width 20 cm, and height 15 cm. Find the surface area of cardboard needed."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Solution:",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " A box with no lid has only 5 faces (no top)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "$$\\begin{aligned} SA &= lw + 2lh + 2wh \\\\ &= (30 \\times 20) + 2(30 \\times 15) + 2(20 \\times 15) \\\\ &= 600 + 900 + 600 \\\\ &= 2100 \\text{ cm}^2 \\end{aligned}$$"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "horizontalRule"
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Common Mistakes"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "table",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "tableRow",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "tableHeader",
                "attrs": {
                  "colspan": 1,
                  "rowspan": 1,
                  "colwidth": null
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Mistake"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "tableHeader",
                "attrs": {
                  "colspan": 1,
                  "rowspan": 1,
                  "colwidth": null
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Why It's Wrong"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "tableHeader",
                "attrs": {
                  "colspan": 1,
                  "rowspan": 1,
                  "colwidth": null
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Correct Approach"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "tableRow",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "attrs": {
                  "colspan": 1,
                  "rowspan": 1,
                  "colwidth": null
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Forgetting a face"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "attrs": {
                  "colspan": 1,
                  "rowspan": 1,
                  "colwidth": null
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Underestimates the total surface area"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "attrs": {
                  "colspan": 1,
                  "rowspan": 1,
                  "colwidth": null
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Count all faces: 6 for cuboid, 5 for triangular prism"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "tableRow",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "attrs": {
                  "colspan": 1,
                  "rowspan": 1,
                  "colwidth": null
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Confusing surface area with volume"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "attrs": {
                  "colspan": 1,
                  "rowspan": 1,
                  "colwidth": null
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Surface area is in cm$^2$; volume is in cm$^3$"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "attrs": {
                  "colspan": 1,
                  "rowspan": 1,
                  "colwidth": null
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "SA involves area of faces; volume fills the inside"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "tableRow",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "attrs": {
                  "colspan": 1,
                  "rowspan": 1,
                  "colwidth": null
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Using wrong dimensions for rectangular faces of a prism"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "attrs": {
                  "colspan": 1,
                  "rowspan": 1,
                  "colwidth": null
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Each rectangle uses the prism length and a side of the triangle"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "attrs": {
                  "colspan": 1,
                  "rowspan": 1,
                  "colwidth": null
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Match each triangle side with the prism length"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "tableRow",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "attrs": {
                  "colspan": 1,
                  "rowspan": 1,
                  "colwidth": null
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Forgetting there are two triangular ends"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "attrs": {
                  "colspan": 1,
                  "rowspan": 1,
                  "colwidth": null
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Only counting one end"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "attrs": {
                  "colspan": 1,
                  "rowspan": 1,
                  "colwidth": null
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Always multiply the triangular end area by 2"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "horizontalRule"
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Practice Questions"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Foundation Tier"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "attrs": {
          "start": 1
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Find the surface area of a cuboid with length 10 cm, width 4 cm, and height 3 cm."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "attrs": {
          "start": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Find the surface area of a cube with side length 7 cm."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "attrs": {
          "start": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "A rectangular box measures 25 cm by 15 cm by 10 cm. Find the total surface area."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "attrs": {
          "start": 4
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "A room is 5 m long, 4 m wide, and 2.5 m high. Find the total area of the four walls (ignore doors and windows)."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "attrs": {
          "start": 5
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "A triangular prism has a right-angled triangular cross-section with legs 3 cm and 4 cm (hypotenuse 5 cm) and is 12 cm long. Find the surface area."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "attrs": {
          "start": 6
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "A cube has a surface area of 150 cm$^2$. Find the side length."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Higher Tier"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "attrs": {
          "start": 7
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "A cuboid has a surface area of 340 cm$^2$. Its length is 10 cm and width is 8 cm. Find the height."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "attrs": {
          "start": 8
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "An equilateral triangular prism has triangle sides of 6 cm and length 15 cm. Given that the height of an equilateral triangle with side $s$ is $\\frac{s\\sqrt{3}}{2}$, find the total surface area to 1 decimal place."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "attrs": {
          "start": 9
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "A gift box in the shape of a triangular prism has an isosceles triangle cross-section (base 8 cm, equal sides 5 cm, height 3 cm). The box is 20 cm long. How much wrapping paper is needed (ignore overlaps)?"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "attrs": {
          "start": 10
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Two cubes of side 4 cm are glued together along one face to form a cuboid. Find the surface area of the resulting shape."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "attrs": {
          "start": 11
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "A wooden triangular prism has all 5 faces to be painted. The cross-section is a right triangle with legs 5 cm and 12 cm. The prism is 20 cm long. One tin of paint covers 200 cm$^2$. How many tins are needed?"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "attrs": {
          "start": 12
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "A pentagonal prism has a regular pentagon cross-section with side 4 cm and area $27.5$ cm$^2$. The prism is 10 cm long. Find the total surface area."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "horizontalRule"
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Answers"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "attrs": {
          "start": 1
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "$SA = 2(10 \\times 4 + 10 \\times 3 + 4 \\times 3) = 2(40 + 30 + 12) = 2 \\times 82 = 164$ cm$^2$"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "attrs": {
          "start": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "$SA = 6 \\times 7^2 = 6 \\times 49 = 294$ cm$^2$"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "attrs": {
          "start": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "$SA = 2(25 \\times 15 + 25 \\times 10 + 15 \\times 10) = 2(375 + 250 + 150) = 2 \\times 775 = 1550$ cm$^2$"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "attrs": {
          "start": 4
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Two walls: $2 \\times 5 \\times 2.5 = 25$ m$^2$. Two walls: $2 \\times 4 \\times 2.5 = 20$ m$^2$. Total $= 25 + 20 = 45$ m$^2$."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "attrs": {
          "start": 5
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Two triangles: $2 \\times \\frac{1}{2}(3)(4) = 12$ cm$^2$. Three rectangles: $(3 \\times 12) + (4 \\times 12) + (5 \\times 12) = 36 + 48 + 60 = 144$ cm$^2$. Total $= 12 + 144 = 156$ cm$^2$."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "attrs": {
          "start": 6
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "$6s^2 = 150$, $s^2 = 25$, $s = 5$ cm."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "attrs": {
          "start": 7
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "$2(10 \\times 8 + 10h + 8h) = 340$, $2(80 + 18h) = 340$, $80 + 18h = 170$, $18h = 90$, $h = 5$ cm."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "attrs": {
          "start": 8
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Triangle height $= \\frac{6\\sqrt{3}}{2} = 3\\sqrt{3}$. Triangle area $= \\frac{1}{2}(6)(3\\sqrt{3}) = 9\\sqrt{3} \\approx 15.59$ cm$^2$. Two ends: $31.2$ cm$^2$. Three rectangles: $3 \\times (6 \\times 15) = 270$ cm$^2$. Total $\\approx 31.2 + 270 = 301.2$ cm$^2$."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "attrs": {
          "start": 9
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Two triangles: $2 \\times \\frac{1}{2}(8)(3) = 24$ cm$^2$. Three rectangles: $(8 \\times 20) + (5 \\times 20) + (5 \\times 20) = 160 + 100 + 100 = 360$ cm$^2$. Total $= 384$ cm$^2$."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "attrs": {
          "start": 10
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The cuboid is $8 \\times 4 \\times 4$. $SA = 2(8 \\times 4 + 8 \\times 4 + 4 \\times 4) = 2(32 + 32 + 16) = 2 \\times 80 = 160$ cm$^2$."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "attrs": {
          "start": 11
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Hypotenuse $= \\sqrt{5^2 + 12^2} = \\sqrt{169} = 13$ cm. Two triangles: $2 \\times \\frac{1}{2}(5)(12) = 60$ cm$^2$. Three rectangles: $(5 + 12 + 13) \\times 20 = 30 \\times 20 = 600$ cm$^2$. Total $= 660$ cm$^2$. Tins $= \\lceil 660/200 \\rceil = 4$ tins."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "attrs": {
          "start": 12
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Two pentagons: $2 \\times 27.5 = 55$ cm$^2$. Five rectangles: $5 \\times (4 \\times 10) = 200$ cm$^2$. Total $= 55 + 200 = 255$ cm$^2$."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "horizontalRule"
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Exam Tips"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "List all faces",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " systematically: draw a net if it helps."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "For prisms, surface area = 2 $\\times$ (end face area) + (perimeter of end face) $\\times$ length."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Watch out for "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "open",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " shapes (no lid, no base) -- you may need to exclude one or more faces."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Label your diagram and tick off each face as you calculate its area."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Units are always "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "squared",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " for surface area."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "horizontalRule"
      },
      {
        "type": "quizEmbed",
        "attrs": {
          "quizId": "quiz-surface-area-prisms"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Summary"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Surface area",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " = total area of all external faces."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Cuboid:",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " $SA = 2(lw + lh + wh)$"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Cube:",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " $SA = 6s^2$"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Triangular prism:",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " $SA = 2 \\times$ (triangle area) + (perimeter of triangle) $\\times$ length"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "General prism:",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " $SA = 2 \\times$ (cross-section area) + (perimeter of cross-section) $\\times$ length"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Always count all faces, including both ends."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
